re and it's it's not  surprising it took people a minute  because you're talking about a really  really big powerful show going on at  that point and do you think that it was  easy to get out it was a pretty wide  open space I mean it's this major open  lot out there and it's pretty easy yeah  it's it easy to get to get out more than  other places that we play it would be  easier than say perhaps a stadium like a  football stadium or something because it  was outdoors and pretty wide open thank  goodness but I mean that had so many  people crammed into one place that like  I said it's it's virtually impossible to  stay calm in that situation John in the  time we have remaining I just want to  point out that we talked about country  music fans but also country music that  you do a ton for all sorts of people I  know you're planning for a big benefit  that's to take place next month so that  you can help hurricane victims you're  always doing things for veterans for law  enforcement for people from all over and  so hopefully you guys can all feel the  from all of us back to you as well  absolutely and I can tell you this these  guys do stuff like this to try to keep  the rest of us from doing what we want  to do with our lives and that's not  going to happen and I would expect a  really strong response out of all of  country music as to what happened last  night you know we got it you got to pray  for these folks too you know people say  our thoughts and prayers you actually  need to pray you actually need to speak  to the Lord and say please bring some  comfort to these people because this is  beyond the pale what has happened and  thank you for your time tonight we  certainly appreciate it

